[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I've been struggling with proving theorems involving SimpleGraph.Walks due to the strict type checking. As I understand it, when comparing two Walks we need to ensure that the types of both of them are the same, which includes the Walks starting and ending at the same vertices. This constraint makes it so that I'm unable to prove theorems like: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">drop_one_cons</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In fact this doesn't even compile properly, I get the error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getVert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The solution recommended by AI is to rewrite the theorem as: <code>p = ((p.cons e).drop 1).copy (SimpleGraph.Walk.snd_cons p e) rfl</code>, which I find unsatisfactory. And even after rewriting it this way I am unable to solve it, the proof gets stuck on <code>p = (p.copy ⋯ ⋯).copy ⋯ ⋯</code>.</p>\n<p>When I tried to prove the same equality inside another proof I used dependent casts to make it compile properly, so it looks like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getVert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">edrop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- proof gets stuck here at ⊢ p = ⋯ ▸ p.copy ⋯ ⋯</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>All of the workarounds I've been recommended by AI till now have been pretty useless and end up with the same issue one way or another. I would like to prove the equality as-is instead of proving something like <code>∀ (k : ℕ), p.getVert k = ((p.cons e).drop 1).getVert k</code> because I want to use it in a <code>rw</code> afterwards.</p>\n<p>Any help regarding this would be much appreciated. Even if there's no way to prove <code>edrop</code>, if there are workarounds to achieve the same thing in some other way it would help me complete my proof.</p>",
        "id": 625450421,
        "sender_full_name": "Ramanuj Goel",
        "timestamp": 1789840660
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>can you provide a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>?</p>",
        "id": 625451069,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1789840956
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah you have to use <code>copy</code>, or <code>HEq</code> (<code>≍</code>) instead of equality</p>",
        "id": 625451192,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841012
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There have been suggestions about introducing a <code>Walk</code> type without endpoints in the type (<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"252551\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/252551-graph-theory/topic/New.20Walk.20definition.20without.20index.20parameters/with/576140776\">#graph theory &gt; New Walk definition without index parameters</a>), but there are pros and cons</p>",
        "id": 625451402,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>does using <code>HEq</code> allow using the proof in a <code>rw</code>?</p>",
        "id": 625451459,
        "sender_full_name": "Ramanuj Goel",
        "timestamp": 1789841156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, <code>copy</code> does. What's the bigger context where you need this theorem for?</p>",
        "id": 625451520,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw this theorem is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=SimpleGraph.Walk.tail_cons#doc\">docs#SimpleGraph.Walk.tail_cons</a></p>",
        "id": 625451587,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841232
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Was trying to prove something like \"if a tree has a diameter of odd length then every diameter shares the middle edge\". I'm sure the proof can be reformatted to not require the above theorem, but that would come at the cost of convenience.</p>",
        "id": 625451764,
        "sender_full_name": "Ramanuj Goel",
        "timestamp": 1789841342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, you can prove it with <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backward</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respectTransparency</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">types</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">drop_one_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">copy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop_cons_eq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 625451855,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789841400
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! That works for me.</p>",
        "id": 625452012,
        "sender_full_name": "Ramanuj Goel",
        "timestamp": 1789841490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What's wrong with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=SimpleGraph.Walk.tail_cons#doc\">docs#SimpleGraph.Walk.tail_cons</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 625452035,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841505
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>tail_cons should also work here, but was generally looking for something that I can use later on as well if I encounter the same problem and don't have a predefined solution.</p>",
        "id": 625452127,
        "sender_full_name": "Ramanuj Goel",
        "timestamp": 1789841563
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would advertise <code>rw!</code></p>",
        "id": 625452707,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1789841935
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't understand what \"something\" you're referring to in the code above, but anyways here's a proof without <code>backward</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">drop_one_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">copy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(but you should really use <code>.tail</code> instead of <code>.drop 1</code>)</p>",
        "id": 625452714,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789841940
    }
]